<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Stavropol Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Stavropol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Soviet republic centred on Stavropol during the first months of the Russian Civil War in 1918.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In early 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> and proclaimed the Stavropol Soviet Republic as an autonomous part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. It was one of several regional Soviet republics declared in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> as the old administration collapsed.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governed by a council of people's commissars, the republic covered the grain lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a>, where the peasants were largely Russian and Ukrainian settlers. It requisitioned grain and organised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia">Red Guard</a> units to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> and anti-Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>. Little is known of its internal administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1918 it was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-caucasian-soviet-republic">North Caucasian Soviet Republic</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a> later that year, and Soviet power returned only in 1920. The territory was later absorbed into the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> Krai.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/stavropol-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Stavropol Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Stavropol</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Stavropol SR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=stavropol-soviet-republic" aria-label="Stavropol Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5679 587 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Stavropol Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5999 843L5820 533M5999 843L6032 874"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M6032 874h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5999 843h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5999 843h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Stavropol. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=stavropol-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
